## Summary
Sungkyul University's G-LAMP project group has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in the United States to collaborate on artificial intelligence and biological convergence research. This international partnership aims to advance interdisciplinary studies at the intersection of technology and medicine. The MOU signifies a commitment to fostering innovation in medical research through AI and bio-related advancements.

## Key Points
- MOU signed between Sungkyul University G-LAMP project group and Cedars-Sinai Medical Center.
- Research focus on AI and bio-convergence, combining technology with biological sciences.
- International collaboration to promote interdisciplinary medical research.
- Potential for developing innovative solutions in healthcare and technology.


